QEC-ADA is an independent Ada/SPARK implementation project. Its initial native
GF(3) kernel, CLI and browser GUI are new work, not a mechanical source port.

Historical QEC research documentation has been copied without byte changes
from QSOLKCB/QEC, source commit 27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d, under docs/reference/qec/.
The files retain the licence and attribution applicable at the source. Original
Git blob SHA-1 values and exclusions are in fixtures/qec_reference_manifest.json.

QEC-ADA makes no representation that archived QEC experiments, third-party
packages, hardware measurements, or historical decoder capabilities have been
implemented, proved, or reproduced by this new project.

For QEC provenance, see docs/reference/qec/CITATION_AND_ATTRIBUTION.md and
the donor repository's LICENCE and NOTICE records. Where a cited historical
reference requires a source path, interpret it relative to the pinned QEC
commit, not the QEC-ADA repository root.

The fixed cyclic [[5,1,3]]_3 qutrit decoder is an independently written Ada
implementation of the mathematical model and bounded enumeration in QEC
src/qec/decoder/qutrit/{gf3,stabilizer,codes,exact}.py at
27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d, under MPL-2.0.

The precomputed one-site contributions and identity-site skipping adapt
the general mechanisms OPT-INV-001 and OPT-REDUCE-001 from QSOLKCB/OPT,
Apache-2.0. No OPT source is copied. There is no universal performance
claim. The new classical selector follows QEC Strowger's first-free
ordering concept but does not claim complete Strowger equivalence or receipts.

Phase 1B introduces a new bounded, independently written Ada implementation
of configurable GF(3) stabilizer-code validation, radius-one exact
syndrome lookup and immutable code-definition-bound OPT contributions.
The algorithm references QEC's public qutrit finite-field and coset-leader
models at 27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d.
No third-party source copied from OPT or Python donor.

Phase 1C uses research design context from multimodalas/fusion-qec
commit a390f57d3da2647ef8d835a7407ad0eb03d03093 (CC BY 4.0),
QSOLKCB/SPECTRAL commit 49401fa010ed673e3d3977ccd5e06d66b0d65096 (MIT), and
QSOLKCB/QEC Strowger source at commit
27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d (MPL-2.0).
The Tanner graph, non-backtracking fourth moment and native
classical switching pilot are independently implemented; no donor
source is copied. Credit and scopes are recorded in
docs/PHASE1C_TANNER_SPECTRAL.md.

Phase 1D independently implements sparse Tanner non-backtracking
spectral diagnostics under QEC-ADA's MPL-2.0 licence. Source inspiration:
QSOLKCB/QEC at 27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d
(MPL-2.0), multimodalas/fusion-qec at
a390f57d3da2647ef8d835a7407ad0eb03d03093 (CC BY 4.0),
QSOLKCB/SPECTRAL at 49401fa010ed673e3d3977ccd5e06d66b0d65096
(MIT), and QSOLKCB/OPT at
7556dd36acd53ed3ed538fd03b1db44e5c1ec869 (Apache-2.0).
No implementation code copied from any donor repository.

Phase 1E extends QEC-ADA with independently implemented MPL-2.0
sparse native Ada spectral analysis and a deterministic synthetic
classical GF(2) min-sum BP research harness. It references mathematical
and engineering ideas from QSOLKCB/QEC
(27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d),
multimodalas/fusion-qec
(a390f57d3da2647ef8d835a7407ad0eb03d03093, CC BY 4.0),
QSOLKCB/SPECTRAL
(49401fa010ed673e3d3977ccd5e06d66b0d65096, MIT), and
QSOLKCB/OPT
(7556dd36acd53ed3ed538fd03b1db44e5c1ec869, Apache-2.0).
No upstream implementation code is copied. The classical BP experiment
does not claim equivalence with QEC's protected decoder.

Phase 1F adds original MPL-2.0 Python-standard-library graph-blocked
inference, canonical evidence replay and a controlled reference-source
runner. The latter *executes, but does not copy into QEC-ADA*, the
`bp_decode` implementation in QSOLKCB/QEC
commit 27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d,
Git blob 266dc35c7162adf6a895eb796760e2bc6724eff4.
That executable donor remains governed by its original repository
license and is only activated via explicit opt-in with its separately
installed NumPy dependency.

Phase 1G adds independently written MPL-2.0 source-bound research
admission and evaluation around QEC's existing `create_code` and
`bp_decode` at commit
27bbc798c4e38138ca5b0fff70b15c3271a1917d,
Git blob 266dc35c7162adf6a895eb796760e2bc6724eff4.
The original QEC module is **executed on explicit opt-in** in a
separate pinned checkout; no QEC code is copied into QEC-ADA.
CSS protograph attribution remains with QEC and its original
references. Native mathematical, routing and sonification source
files are not changed by this Phase 1G adapter.

Phase 1H introduces independently written MPL-2.0 strict parsing,
exact GF(2) CSS validation, publisher-blocked evaluation and
source-bound replay for public, independently maintained
parity-check matrices. No original data file or source implementation
from these projects is copied into this repository.

Source A: NISQEC: Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum Error Correction
by Eugenio Durazo Rocha, Olai A. Mostad, Hsuan-Yin Lin and Eirik
Rosnes, 2026, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23378284, licensed CC BY 4.0;
pinned Simula-UiB/nisqec commit
913e0f26b07919ab73d7052159196599d34a2969.

Source B: Check-weight-constrained quantum codes: Bounds and examples,
public QLDPC matrix collection by Lily Wang, Andy Zeyi Liu,
Ray Li, Aleksander Kubica and Shouzhen Gu, pinned
lilyxy/Check-weight-constrained-quantum-codes commit
0e6c3e281fe044315286fbdcf5295cb16f47f90d.
No repository licence is identified for Source B. QEC-ADA
neither redistributes its raw matrices nor asserts a licence
to do so. Source Git blobs and attribution are recorded in
fixtures/phase1h_external_css_sources.json. QEC's separate,
opt-in pinned BP reference remains under its original licence.

Phase 1I's independent MPL-2.0 Python-standard-library CSS Pauli
syndrome decoder and exact GF(2) stabilizer-coset classifier use
previously pinned Phase 1H matrix source definitions only,
without copying data-provider implementations or raw parity
matrices. Source rights, authors and exact Git blob IDs are
attributed in fixtures/phase1h_external_css_sources.json and
docs/PHASE1H_EXTERNAL_CSS.md. The explicitly unlicensed
external matrix collection remains read-only and is **not**
redistributed by the Phase 1I code or CI artifacts.
The native Ada GF(3) mathematical code and third-party
QEC reference executable are unchanged and not dependencies
of the Phase 1I pure mathematical decoder.
